  "summary": "Full assessment of all 419 Bengali/Vietnamese passages: three act headings, every speech and every stage direction, translated directly from the Bengali Wikisource transcription. The first reviews scored 8.73 (Act I), 8.48 (Act II) and 8.38 (Act III) and found three majors (the scholars motif rendered inconsistently, an hour-count that contradicted the king’s midnight arrival, and the royal physician mislabelled); one round of fixes and fresh separate-context blind reviews of the failing ranges then scored 9.05 (Act II) and 8.63 (Act III), with Act I already at 8.73, and no major or critical finding open. The final score is taken from the weakest range, 8.63 on the half-point scale, above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. Open minors include a stiff logic line in unit 321, an added detail in unit 382 and a stilted question in unit 400.",
  "title_review": {
    "source_title": "ডাকঘর",
    "target_title": "Bưu điện",
    "rationale": "The title is translated as ‘Bưu điện’; no earlier Vietnamese title was checked."
  }
}
